@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@code{dired-video-thumbnail} is an Emacs package that provides @code{image-dired}
style thumbnail viewing for video files. It extracts thumbnails from videos using
@command{ffmpeg} and displays them in a grid layout, allowing you to visually
browse and manage video collections directly from Emacs.

@section Features

@itemize @bullet
@item
Thumbnail grid display with configurable layout
@item
Persistent caching - thumbnails are cached and only regenerated when the source
file changes
@item
Asynchronous generation - Emacs remains responsive while thumbnails are generated
in the background
@item
Dired integration - marks sync bidirectionally with the associated dired buffer
@item
Visual mark indication - marked thumbnails display a colored border (like @code{image-dired})
@item
Dynamic header line - shows filename, dimensions, duration, and file size for the
current video
@item
Click to play - open videos in your preferred external player
@item
Cross-platform - works on Linux, macOS, and Windows
@item
Resizable thumbnails - adjust thumbnail size on the fly
@item
Recursive search - optionally search for videos in subdirectories
@item
Sorting and filtering - organize videos by name, date, size, or duration
@end itemize

