@node Requirements
@section Requirements

Before installing @code{dired-video-thumbnail}, ensure you have:

@itemize @bullet
@item
Emacs 28.1 or later
@item
@command{ffmpeg} and @command{ffprobe} installed and available in your @env{PATH}
@end itemize

To verify @command{ffmpeg} is installed, run:

@example
ffmpeg -version
@end example

@node Manual Installation
@section Manual Installation

Download @file{dired-video-thumbnail.el} and place it in your load path:

@lisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "/path/to/dired-video-thumbnail/")
(require 'dired-video-thumbnail)
@end lisp

@node Package Manager
@section Installing via Package Managers

@subsection use-package

@lisp
(use-package dired-video-thumbnail
  :load-path "/path/to/dired-video-thumbnail/"
  :bind (:map dired-mode-map
         ("C-t v" . dired-video-thumbnail)))
@end lisp

@subsection straight.el

@lisp
(straight-use-package
 '(dired-video-thumbnail :type git :host github
   :repo "captainflasmr/dired-video-thumbnail"))
@end lisp

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

@section Basic Usage

@enumerate
@item
Open a directory containing video files in dired
@item
Run @kbd{M-x dired-video-thumbnail}
@item
A new buffer opens displaying thumbnails for all videos in the directory
@item
The cursor automatically moves to the first thumbnail
@end enumerate

@section Working with Marked Files

@enumerate
@item
In dired, mark specific video files with @kbd{m}
@item
Run @kbd{M-x dired-video-thumbnail}
@item
Only thumbnails for the marked videos are displayed
@end enumerate

@section Suggested Keybinding

Add a keybinding in dired for quick access:

@lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'dired
  (define-key dired-mode-map (kbd "C-t v") #'dired-video-thumbnail))
@end lisp

@section Header Line Information

As you navigate between thumbnails, the header line dynamically displays
information about the current video:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{Mark indicator} - A red asterisk if the video is marked
@item
@strong{Filename} - The video filename in bold
@item
@strong{Dimensions} - Video resolution (e.g., 1920x1080)
@item
@strong{Duration} - Video length (e.g., 5:32 or 1:23:45)
@item
@strong{File size} - Size in MB (e.g., 45.2 MB)
@end itemize

@node Keybindings
@chapter Keybindings

All commands are available in the @code{*Video Thumbnails*} buffer.

@section Navigation Commands

@table @kbd
@item n
@itemx p
@itemx @key{SPC}
Move to next/previous thumbnail (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-next},
@code{dired-video-thumbnail-previous})

@item @key{right}
@itemx @key{left}
@itemx C-f
@itemx C-b
Move forward/backward to adjacent thumbnail (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-forward},
@code{dired-video-thumbnail-backward})

@item @key{up}
@itemx @key{down}
Move up/down one row (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-previous-row},
@code{dired-video-thumbnail-next-row})

@item d
Switch to associated dired buffer (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-goto-dired})

@item q
Close the thumbnail buffer (@code{quit-window})
@end table

@section Playback Commands

@table @kbd
@item @key{RET}
@itemx mouse-1
Play video at point (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-play})
@end table

On Linux, videos open with @command{xdg-open}. On macOS, they open with
@command{open}. On Windows, they open with the system default player.

@section Marking Commands

Marks are synchronized with the associated dired buffer. Marking a video in
the thumbnail view also marks it in dired, and vice versa.

@table @kbd
@item m
Mark video and move to next (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-mark})

@item u
Unmark video and move to next (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-unmark})

@item mouse-3
Toggle mark on video under mouse (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-toggle-mark})

@item M
Mark all videos (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-mark-all})

@item U
Unmark all videos (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-unmark-all})

@item t
Invert all marks (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-toggle-all-marks})
@end table

@section Deletion Commands

@table @kbd
@item D
Delete video at point with confirmation (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-delete})

@item x
Delete marked videos with confirmation (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-delete-marked})
@end table

@section Display Commands

@table @kbd
@item +
@itemx -
Increase/decrease thumbnail size (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-increase-size},
@code{dired-video-thumbnail-decrease-size})

@item r
Refresh the display (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-refresh})

@item g
Regenerate thumbnail for video at point (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-regenerate})

@item G
Regenerate all thumbnails (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-regenerate-all})

@item R
Toggle recursive search (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-toggle-recursive})

@item w
Toggle wrap display mode (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-toggle-wrap})
@end table

@section Sorting Commands

Sorting commands are prefixed with @kbd{s}:

@table @kbd
@item s n
Sort by name (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-sort-by-name})

@item s d
Sort by date modified (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-sort-by-date})

@item s s
Sort by file size (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-sort-by-size})

@item s D
Sort by duration (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-sort-by-duration})

@item s r
Reverse sort order (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-sort-reverse})

@item S
Interactive sort selection (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-sort})
@end table

@section Filtering Commands

Filtering commands are prefixed with @kbd{/}:

@table @kbd
@item / n
Filter by filename regexp (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-filter-by-name})

@item / d
Filter by duration range (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-filter-by-duration})

@item / s
Filter by file size range (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-filter-by-size})

@item / /
@itemx / c
Clear all filters (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-filter-clear})

@item \
Interactive filter selection (@code{dired-video-thumbnail-filter})
@end table

